WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.650
Things look bleak for Tony Stark in the Avengers:
Endgame trailer, but Iron Man has been in

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.660
some pretty tight squeezes before.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.900
Endgame's cast includes spacefarers, gods,
wizards, interstellar warlords, and more.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.940
In all likelihood, Stark's rescue isn't a
question of if, but of who and when.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:22.400
Tony spends the Avengers: Endgame trailer
leaving a final message for his one true love,

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.220
Pepper Potts.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.500
So it's only fitting that it will probably
be Pepper who saves him.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.740
Not only would it be an emotionally satisfying
payoff, it also makes sense.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.900
Pepper was talking to Tony when he left Earth,
so she knows where to start the search.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.180
As the CEO of Stark Industries, she has the
resources to mount a rescue, and as Tony's

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.420
fiancee, she certainly has the motive.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.880
Plus, we've seen her rescue him before, in
Iron Man 3.

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:49.790
Perhaps the biggest clue, though, is the fact
that leaks from the set of Avengers: Endgame

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.240
suggested that Pepper would be donning her
own suit of armor for the film.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.920
That's something she's done in the comics,
where her superhero codename is…

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:57.780
Rescue.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.719
"Just for the record, being adrift in space
with zero promise of rescue is more fun than

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:04.220
it sounds."

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.880
Yeah, it seems pretty obvious when we put
it that way!

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.980
When Thanos snapped his fingers and caused
the Decimation, the only two warriors on distant

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.960
Titan left alive were Tony Stark and Nebula.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.760
It's unclear whether Nebula is on the ship
with Tony in the Endgame trailer.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.460
But it would make sense if she ended up saving
Tony.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:25.860
After all, she has plenty of experience flying
these super advanced spacecraft, plus she

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.840
may be able to use her status as a cyborg
to help repair the ship.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.520
We know she will want revenge on Thanos for
the death of Gamora, and saving Tony may just

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:35.180
help her get it.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.180
After the heartbreaking loss of Groot at the
end of Avengers: Infinity War, Rocket was

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.920
essentially left alone on Earth.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.560
It would make sense if he left to find out
the fate of the rest of his Guardians of the

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:46.579
Galaxy family.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:51.119
Unfortunately, they were all snapped out of
existence back on Titan, but if Rocket goes

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.460
searching for them, he could very well find
Tony instead.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.479
Thor and Tony Stark aren't best friends, but
they are both founding Avengers, and the Odinson

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.000
isn't going to leave Stark hanging if he can
help it.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.680
Thanks to his new hammer Stormbreaker, Thor
seems to be able to access the Bifrost and

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.260
teleport vast distances across space.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.760
If he goes looking for Stark - perhaps with
the help of his new sidekick Rocket - Stormbreaker

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.660
could help him get there in the nick of time.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.820
Tony isn't the only refugee set adrift in
space due to the evil of Thanos.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.680
There's also half of the Asgardians who were
attacked at the end of Thor: Ragnarok.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:30.080
Endgame director Joe Russo has said that Valkyrie
survived the attack, and fans certainly hope

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.700
that scene-stealing favorite Korg also survived.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.180
It would be fitting, and thrilling, if Valkyrie
and Korg showed up in the nick of time to

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.140
rescue Tony.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:43.920
After Wong saved Tony from certain death in
Avengers: Infinity War, the two became instant

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:44.720
best buds.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.200
"Wong, you're invited to my wedding!"

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.100
So can Wong do it again?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.840
In Infinity War, Doctor Strange seems pretty
nervous about Stark's ability to get them

00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:02.839
back to Earth, implying that he couldn't do
it with magic.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:03.420
But why not?

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.900
If wizards can step between dimensions, why
not between planets?

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.739
Sure, they need to visualize their destination,
but if Tony is able to get a video SOS back

00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:16.269
to Earth, maybe Wong can open a portal with
his sling ring and get them both back to the

00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:17.260
church in time.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.040
Captain Marvel was nowhere to be seen in the
Avengers: Endgame trailer, but thanks to the

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:26.700
Avengers: Infinity War post-credits teaser,
we know she'll be an important part of Endgame.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.800
And we know from the Captain Marvel trailer
that she can soar through the spaceways under

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:31.760
her own power.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.840
What better way to introduce her to the Avengers
than by having her save Tony Stark?

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.960
Things look pretty dire for Tony in the Endgame
trailer.

00:03:38.969 --> 00:03:42.559
But things have looked pretty bad for him
before, and he's managed to work miracles

00:03:42.559 --> 00:03:43.559
with far less.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.680
"Tony Stark was able to build this in a cave!

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.040
With a box of scraps!"

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:54.720
So it would be no surprise if Tony suddenly
got a flash of brilliance that allowed him

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.680
to save himself.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.440
After losing everything in the fight against
Thanos, it seems as though his confidence

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.940
is at an all time low.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.360
But maybe his love for Pepper will be enough
to shake him out of his stupor so he can fix

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.460
his spaceship and get home in once piece.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.420
The shockingly bleak end of Avengers: Infinity
War had many fans in tears.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.980
But what if Marvel saved the worst blow for
last?

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:20.079
Maybe what we see in this trailer is exactly
what we're going to get: Tony, alone in space,

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.980
drifting off into oblivion, never to be seen
again.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.300
Would it be disappointing?

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:24.940
Yes.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.140
Devastating?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:26.820
Sure.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:27.940
But is it likely?

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:29.460
Well, probably not.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:33.580
But after the way they killed off poor Peter
Parker, we wouldn't put anything past those

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.220
monsters.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.020
"I'm sorry!"

